<%# The summary half of the warning, in a wrapper that is **always rendered**.

    It has to exist even when there is nothing to say, because `turbo_stream.replace` needs an element
    with that id to replace. Without it the warning could appear on load and never leave: correcting the
    days fixed the data and the notification kept accusing you until a full reload. Reported exactly that
    way, and it is the same staleness I had just fixed for the Earns figures in the very same change -
    the callout is derived from the same entries and I did not carry the rule across.

    An entry claiming the perfect-attendance bonus with no days recorded is incoherent whatever the
    quarter's length, so this needs no school-days figure - the number the app does not store. %>
<% affected = earnings.unattended_bonus_entries %>

<div id="unattended-bonus-callout">
  <% if affected.any? %>
    <div class="mb-6">
      <%= render "components/ui/callout",
                 title: "#{pluralize(affected.size, 'student')} set to be paid a bonus with no attendance recorded",
                 body: "#{affected.map { |e| e.user.display_name }.to_sentence} " \
                       "#{affected.one? ? 'is' : 'are'} marked as having perfect attendance but " \
                       "#{affected.one? ? 'has' : 'have'} no days entered. Finalizing pays the " \
                       "#{number_to_currency(GradeEntry::EARNINGS_FOR_PERFECT_ATTENDANCE / 100.0)} " \
                       "bonus anyway." %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
